showcase (https://github.com/tudorjuravlea/showcase), MIT License, by the same author.
Adapted into scripts/lib/ffmpeg.mjs, scripts/lib/sheet.mjs, scripts/stills.mjs, scripts/export.mjs and
scripts/lib/standalone.mjs: the seek-then-screenshot frame loop piped to ffmpeg, the explicit BT.709
matrix and tv-range colour recipe, the contact sheet composed in a second headless page, the
dry-run-before-render habit, the order-independence determinism proof, and the lesson that a
fixed-length picture needs its audio padded or trimmed to it.

Derived in shape, not copied: patterns/devices/phone, patterns/devices/browser,
patterns/devices/laptop and patterns/devices/screen-zoom take abstract device proportions (aspect
ratio, bezel and corner radius, lid angle) and redraw them as generic CSS boxes; patterns/moves/hero-drift
takes the float look's amplitudes and the hero-pose idea, scaled down and re-expressed as a pure
function of progress on a DOM camera; patterns/moves/orbit takes the orbit look (a turn about Y with
a smaller X sway) with reduced amplitudes.

